lent computer skills, can be grumpy, can be uncooperative.\n\nC: makes correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew, keeps calm in crisis (stress resilience), maybe also decision quality (quick correct decisions). Reliability strong, crew cooperation positive, but communication difficulty, egocentric, low adaptability.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership, considered arrogant.\n\nWe need to evaluate against criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention/accuracy, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility/maturity, adaptability/feedback.\n\nWe have evidence for each.\n\nNow we need to give a concise contribution: maybe propose initial recommendation based on overall fit. Let's weigh:\n\nReliability: C is 100% reliable. Others unknown.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well, C keeps calm in crisis, D responds adequately, A unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision; B good at assessing weather, computer skills; C makes correct decisions quickly; D solves problems extremely well.\n\nDecision quality: C quick correct decisions; A anticipates dangerous situations; D responds adequately.\n\nAttention: D concentrates well; A maybe unorganized; B unknown.\n\nCrew cooperation: C creates positive atmosphere; B can be uncooperative; D arrogant; A leadership but maybe not good at criticism.\n\nCommunication: C difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric; B can be grumpy; D arrogant; A not good at taking criticism.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; A leadership; B conscientious; C reliable.\n\nAdaptability: B unknown; C low; D weak leadership; A not good at criticism.\n\nOverall, C has strong reliability, crew cooperation, decision quality, stress resilience, but communication issues and low adaptability.\n\nB has stress resilience, conscientious, but uncooperative and grumpy.\n\nA has leadership, anticipation, but unorganized, poor at criticism.\n\nD has responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but arrogance, weak leadership.\n\nGiven safety-critical role, reliability and crew cooperation are crucial. Communication also vital. C's communication difficulty and egocentric may be a concern. B's uncooperative also concerning. A's unorganized and poor at criticism may affect safety. D's arrogance and weak leadership also concerning.\n\nProbably C is strongest overall despite communication issues, but we need to discuss. I can propose provisional recommendation for Candidate C, noting concerns about communication and adaptability.\n\nAlso note missing evidence: technical competence for D, B, A; attention for B; crew cooperation for A, B, D; professional communication for D; adaptability for B, D.\n\nWe could ask other panel members for observations on Candidate B's crew cooperation and communication, or Candidate D's leadership and communication.\n\nBut as first contribution, I can share my provisional recommendation and highlight evidence and concerns.\n\nThus public message: I recommend Candidate C, citing reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but note communication and adaptability concerns. Also note missing info for others.\n\nVote: Candidate C."}
